<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Władysław III of Poland</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1424">1424</a>–<a href="/years/1444">1444</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Vladislaus I of Hungary, Władysław Warneńczyk · Of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jagiellonian-dynasty">Jagiellonian dynasty</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Władysław III was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> from 1434 and, as Vladislaus I, king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> from 1440 until his death. His election in Hungary against the infant Ladislaus V led to civil war, but with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-hunyadi">John Hunyadi</a> he waged the Long Campaign against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> in 1443–1444. He was killed at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-varna">Battle of Varna</a> in 1444, earning the name Warneńczyk, 'of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/varna">Varna</a>'.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wladyslaw-iii-of-poland.jpg" alt="Władysław III of Poland" width="320" height="380" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:W%C5%82adys%C5%82aw_Warne%C5%84czyk_seal_1438_(cropped).PNG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Sigismund's crusading army was crushed at the Battle of Nicopolis in 1396, and King <b>Vladislaus I</b> fell at the Battle of Varna in 1444.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-hungary-1301-1526">Kingdom of Hungary (1301-1526) · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>According to the historian Jan Długosz, Polish knights sang it at the Battle of Grunwald in 1410 and before other notable battles in the years that followed; it also accompanied the coronation of <b>Władysław III of Poland</b> and of the first Jagiellonian kings.</blockquote><a href="/songs/bogurodzica">Bogurodzica (Mother of God)</a></li><li><blockquote>King <b>Władysław III of Poland</b> and Hungary was killed, and the defeat ended the Crusade of Varna.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/november-10">10 November in history</a></li></ul></section>
